{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":10,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_full_alternation_impossible_of_lt_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_full_alternation_impossible_of_lt_two","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L112-L121","doc":"**At any `q < 2` — every physical substrate value — no solution of the GGM recurrence\nalternates at every level.** The hypothesis of `twoOp_residual_kills_residue` cannot be\nsupplied by the corpus's Door-v carrier; only the from-level-`n₀` form can. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_full_alternation_forces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_full_alternation_forces","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L103-L110","doc":"**Full `(−1)^m` alternation forces `2 ≤ q^(m+1)` at every `m`.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_solution_no_double_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_solution_no_double_flip","kind":"theorem","line":92,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L92-L101","doc":"A solution of the GGM recurrence cannot flip at two consecutive pairs while the\ncoefficient is positive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_flip_after_same","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_flip_after_same","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L88-L90","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_no_double_flip","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggm_no_double_flip","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L84-L86","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggmCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.ggmCoeff","kind":"def","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L81-L82","doc":"The GGM coefficient `2 − q^(m+1)` at index `m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.flip_persists_of_lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.flip_persists_of_lt","kind":"theorem","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L64-L77","doc":"**A flip persists once `|a| < −c · |b|`** (which itself forces `c < 0` and `b ≠ 0`). This\nis why the strict alternation, once the growing solution dominates, never stops. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.flip_after_same_of_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.flip_after_same_of_neg","kind":"theorem","line":56,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L56-L62","doc":"**Negative coefficient: a same-sign pair is followed by a flip.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.no_double_flip_of_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.no_double_flip_of_pos","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L49-L54","doc":"**Positive coefficient: a flip is followed by a same-sign pair.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.GGMAlternationOnset.step","kind":"def","line":46,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/GGMAlternationOnset.lean#L46-L47","doc":"One step of the three-term recurrence `y (m+2) = c · y (m+1) − y m`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}